From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 07:52:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05027/11362] [outer-loop] PHASE D RESULT: trained
 oracle-distinct verifier does NOT beat SC on MuSR (bounded null)

The decisive moat experiment the conductor's D1/D2 could not run (404 base + empty logprob cache).
Outer-loop bootstrap on GPU-1: regenerated 200-q MuSR reasoning traces (Qwen3.5-9B-MTP), trained a
k-fold leakage-safe oracle-distinct verifier (all-MiniLM embed -> logistic head over question+reasoning),
tested vs genuine SC.

RESULT: verifier 0.570 vs SC 0.555, delta +0.015 CI95 [-0.06,0.085] (includes 0), McNemar p=0.78 ->
verifier_beats_sc=False. Despite oracle@K=0.925 (0.37 of headroom), the trained verifier captures ~none.
moat_realized=False -> HONEST BOUNDED NULL, converging with the ARC verifier-tie: even a trained
oracle-distinct verifier on reasoning-text embeddings cannot capture MuSR headroom. DiffusionGemma stays
gated. verifier_is_oracle=False, headroom_present=True, paired CI -> B2-moat-lint compliant.

Caveat: this is a simple embedding-head verifier; the full LoRA-EBM might differ, but the signal is strong
(reasoning-text embeddings don't linearly separate correct from incorrect on MuSR).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
